{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_x3fljazodzuvnfsgmnoty2okapqe5c4y43mpcbpamest74s6k2ca","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01RtQz8YDgAUXMrNjLrFcqw9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > tests/alloc_wraparound.rs <<'HEADER'\n//! Phase C — the allocation-failure rejection branches reached *deterministically*\n//! through the C's own integer arithmetic (`ERRORS.md` rows 3, 3b and 4).\n//!\n//! `int l = strlen(src) + 1;` (`lib.c:49`) truncates to `int`. For\n//! `strlen(src) == 4294967282` that makes `l == -13`, so\n//!\n//!   * `calloc(sizeof(char), l + 13)` becomes `calloc(1, 0)` — which SUCCEEDS,\n//!   * and the following `malloc(l)` converts `-13` to `(size_t)0xFFFF…F3` —\n//!     which ALWAYS fails.\n//!\n//! i.e. row 4 (`free(dest); return NULL`) is reached with no environment\n//! trickery at all. `l <= -14` instead makes `l + 13` negative, so `calloc`\n//! itself gets a huge `size_t` and fails: row 3.\n//!\n//! These tests need multi-GiB buffers, which is why they live in their own test\n//! binary: freeing such a buffer leaves a huge reusable hole in the heap that\n//! would perturb the `RLIMIT_AS` tests in `alloc_failure.rs`.\n\nmod common;\n\nuse common::diff_null;\nuse std::ffi::c_char;\n\nfn mem_available_bytes() -> u64 {\n    let s = std::fs::read_to_string(\"/proc/meminfo\").unwrap_or_default();\n    for line in s.lines() {\n        if let Some(rest) = line.strip_prefix(\"MemAvailable:\") {\n            if let Some(kb) = rest.split_whitespace().next() {\n                if let Ok(v) = kb.parse::<u64>() {\n                    return v * 1024;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    0\n}\n\nHEADER\npython3 - <<'PY'\ndet = open('tests/_det_part.txt').read()\n# drop the section banner\ndet = det.split('\\n', 3)[3]\nopen('tests/alloc_wraparound.rs','a').write(det)\nPY\nrm tests/_det_part.txt && grep -n \"fn \" tests/alloc_wraparound.rs | head -20 && timeout 300 cargo build --offline --tests 2>&1 | tail -5","description":"Create alloc_wraparound.rs test file"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6518,"cache_read_input_tokens":138650,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6518,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c199c1a9-b8ce-4fd8-b611-969766e92ee3","uuid":"1239c70b-66a2-4900-8fbb-0a8d761dad6d","timestamp":"2026-08-20T08:15:16.332Z"}
